<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia,Africa agree need to withhold more coffee.</title>
<headline>Colombia,Africa agree need to withhold more coffee.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombian coffee officials agreed with their counterparts from the Ivory Coast and Uganda on a need to increase the amount of coffee withheld under the Association of Coffee Producing Countries' export retention plan during the first half of next year by about 2.5 million 60-kilo bags.</p>
<p>The surprise announcement was made after Jorge Cardenas, head of the National Cofffee Growers' Federation, held talks in Bogota Wednesday with Ivorian Commodities Minister Guy-Alain Gauza and Abel Rwendeire of Uganda.</p>
</text>
